	<logo>https://static.globalissues.org/i/globalissues/logo-feed.jpg</logo><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/12/44322</id><title>Navi Pillay’s Nobel Peace Prize Is a Vote of Confidence in a Global Legal Order under Fire</title><updated>2026-10-12T18:35:41-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/12/44322" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/Navy-Pillay___-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;
PRETORIA, South Africa, October 12 (IPS)  - The &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nobelpeaceprize.org/press/press-releases/nobel-peace-prize-for-2026&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;awarding&lt;/a&gt; of the 2026 Nobel Peace Prize to distinguished South African jurist and international judge Navanethem &lt;a href=&quot;https://sahistory.org.za/people/navanethem-navi-pillay&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;“Navi” Pillay&lt;/a&gt; is about more than just the recognition of an exceptional individual in the global fight for justice.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/12/44322&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Navi Pillay’s Nobel Peace Prize Is a Vote of Confidence in a Global Legal Order under Fire”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/12/44318</id><title>How Nepal is Learning To Cope With the Psychological Toll of Its Missing</title><updated>2026-10-12T08:35:13-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/12/44318" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/missing-nepal.png" /><media:content url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/missing-nepal.png" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/missing-nepal.png" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/missing-nepal.png&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;KATHMANDU, October 12 (IPS)  - Nearly three decades ago, in the final stretch of Nepal’s civil war, Dr Brandon Kohrt sat with parents whose sons had been conscripted as child soldiers and never returned.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/12/44318&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “How Nepal is Learning To Cope With the Psychological Toll of Its Missing”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/12/44310</id><title>Kazakhstan Has Spent 23 Years Bringing Faiths Together. Now Comes the Harder Part.</title><updated>2026-10-12T06:44:46-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/12/44310" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/Religious-leaders_121026.jpg" /><media:content url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/Religious-leaders_121026.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/Religious-leaders_121026-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/Religious-leaders_121026.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
ASTANA, Kazakhstan, October 12 (IPS)  - In a world increasingly divided by war, political distrust and competing ideologies, Kazakhstan has spent more than two decades pursuing an unusual diplomatic undertaking: keeping representatives of different religions in conversation.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/12/44310&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Kazakhstan Has Spent 23 Years Bringing Faiths Together. Now Comes the Harder Part.”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/12/44323</id><title>Sudan: Drought and war push Darfur and Kordofan towards famine</title><updated>2026-10-12T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/12/44323" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/10/12-10-2026-UNICEF-Sudan.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/10/12-10-2026-UNICEF-Sudan.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/10/12-10-2026-UNICEF-Sudan.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/10/12-10-2026-UNICEF-Sudan.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The risk of famine is growing in parts of Sudan already torn apart by war, as a severe El Niño drought makes life even harder in Greater Darfur and Greater Kordofan, the UN-backed global hunger monitor warned on Monday.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/12/44323&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Sudan: Drought and war push Darfur and Kordofan towards famine”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/12/44321</id><title>UN aid operation underway in Nepal following fresh floods</title><updated>2026-10-12T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/12/44321" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/09/15-09-2026_UNICEF_Nepal.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/09/15-09-2026_UNICEF_Nepal.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/09/15-09-2026_UNICEF_Nepal.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/09/15-09-2026_UNICEF_Nepal.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The United Nations has rushed to assist Nepal following new flash floods in the central Gorkha district on Sunday that swept away homes and bridges just weeks after catastrophic flooding in the north. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/12/44321&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “UN aid operation underway in Nepal following fresh floods”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/12/44320</id><title>‘Efficiency has limits’: UNHCR chief warns refugee protection is buckling under cuts</title><updated>2026-10-12T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/12/44320" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/09/25-09-2026_UNICEF_Yemen-01.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/09/25-09-2026_UNICEF_Yemen-01.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/09/25-09-2026_UNICEF_Yemen-01.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/09/25-09-2026_UNICEF_Yemen-01.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The money is running out faster than needs are growing: with 117 million men, women and children now forced from their homes, the UN refugee agency (UNHCR) has received just $3 billion of the $8.5 billion it needs this year – and its chief, Barham Salih, warns that the global support system for asylum-seekers risks buckling.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/12/44320&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “‘Efficiency has limits’: UNHCR chief warns refugee protection is buckling under cuts”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/12/44319</id><title>Rise in poverty is ‘a wake-up call for the world’, UN development chief says</title><updated>2026-10-12T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/12/44319" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/08/18-08-2026-UNOCHA-DR-Congo-ebola-03.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/08/18-08-2026-UNOCHA-DR-Congo-ebola-03.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/08/18-08-2026-UNOCHA-DR-Congo-ebola-03.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/08/18-08-2026-UNOCHA-DR-Congo-ebola-03.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The number of people living in “multidimensional” poverty has risen for the first time in 15 years, reaching 1.2 billion, as families struggle to meet their basic needs. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/12/44319&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Rise in poverty is ‘a wake-up call for the world’, UN development chief says”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/11/44317</id><title>Djibouti shipwreck: Death toll rises to 139 as 84 remain missing</title><updated>2026-10-11T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/11/44317" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/07/02-07-2026-IOM-Djibouti-shipwrecked-04.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/07/02-07-2026-IOM-Djibouti-shipwrecked-04.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/07/02-07-2026-IOM-Djibouti-shipwrecked-04.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/07/02-07-2026-IOM-Djibouti-shipwrecked-04.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;At least 139 migrants have died after their boat capsized off Djibouti, with a further 84 people still missing, the UN migration agency (IOM) said on Sunday.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/11/44317&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Djibouti shipwreck: Death toll rises to 139 as 84 remain missing”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/11/44316</id><title>‘These attacks must cease immediately’: Guterres condemns deadly Houthi strike on Riyadh airport</title><updated>2026-10-11T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/11/44316" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production+Library/06-11-2020_Riyadh_Saudi_Arabia_unsplash.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production+Library/06-11-2020_Riyadh_Saudi_Arabia_unsplash.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production+Library/06-11-2020_Riyadh_Saudi_Arabia_unsplash.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production+Library/06-11-2020_Riyadh_Saudi_Arabia_unsplash.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;UN Secretary-General António Guterres has condemned a Houthi missile attack on Riyadh’s main airport that Saudi authorities say killed 12 people and wounded more than 300.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/11/44316&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “‘These attacks must cease immediately’: Guterres condemns deadly Houthi strike on Riyadh airport”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/11/44313</id><title>Sustaining livelihoods amid crisis in Gaza</title><updated>2026-10-11T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/11/44313" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/10/06-10-2026-UNDP-Gaza-04.jpeg/image1440x560cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/10/06-10-2026-UNDP-Gaza-04.jpeg/image1440x560cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/10/06-10-2026-UNDP-Gaza-04.jpeg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/10/06-10-2026-UNDP-Gaza-04.jpeg/image1440x560cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Nidaa, Hanaa and Hanin have different stories, but share a common thread: the determination to build something of their own and keep it going despite extraordinary challenges facing them in war-ravaged Gaza.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/11/44313&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Sustaining livelihoods amid crisis in Gaza”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry></feed><!-- 0.0005s ch:1 -->